{%- comment -%}
  THE CANONICAL NON SOMM ENTRY.

  One component, four surfaces. The pairing page defined this composition and
  is the golden master; this snippet is that composition extracted so the
  homepage and the PDP can RENDER it rather than each rebuilding something
  that resembles it.

  It exists because they did rebuild it. The PDP grew a parallel
  `.non-somm-entry` tree - a <div> where this is a <form>, a `→` glyph where
  this has a real <button type="submit">, its own class names and its own grid
  - and once there were two grids there was a surface with the controls sitting
  in the orb's 96px column and the 663px content column standing empty. That is
  not a styling bug that can be patched. Two components drift; one cannot.

  WHAT THIS OWNS: the DOM structure and the class system. Internal layout comes
  entirely from `.non-somm` in theme.css, which stays the sole owner of the
  grid - 96px minmax(0, 1fr), 44px gap, align-items: start, justify-items
  normal, orb in column 1 spanning the composition, content in column 2.

  WHAT CALLERS MAY CHANGE: copy, context, chips, and outer spacing through
  `modifier`. Nothing else. A caller cannot reach the internal grid, the orb's
  positioning model, the input/button mechanics or the chip mechanics, because
  none of those are parameters. That is the point of the snippet.

  PARAMETERS
    surface       required. Analytics + Worker context: 'homepage_hero',
                  'product_entry'. Sent as data-somm-surface.
    context       required. Conversation context: 'home', 'product'.
    modifier      optional. ONE class for OUTER spacing only, e.g.
                  'non-somm--pdp'. Never for internal layout.
    uid           required. Unique per instance, for the label/input id pair.
                  Two Somms on one page with the same id gives one of them a
                  label pointing at the other's input.
    label         optional. The eyebrow above the bar. Product-aware on a PDP:
                  "Considering NON1?"
    placeholder   required. Also the visually-hidden label text, so the field
                  is never unlabelled even when the eyebrow is absent.
    submit_label  required. The button's words. "Ask" on the hero.
    chips         optional. Newline- or pipe-separated preset prompts.
    product       optional. Passed on a PDP so the conversation knows the
                  bottle without the customer naming it.
    code          optional. The resolved NON code for that product.

  The <form> is real and so is the button: native submission is what makes
  Enter work in the field, what gives the control a submit event to hook, and
  what a screen reader announces as a search. The old PDP div had none of that.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- assign somm_uid = uid | default: 'somm' -%}
{%- assign somm_context = context | default: 'home' -%}
{%- assign somm_surface = surface | default: 'somm_entry' -%}

{%- comment -%}
  Chips accept either separator. The hero's schema uses a pipe list and the
  product settings use one per line; normalising here means neither caller has
  to care, and a caller that supplies neither simply gets no chip row rather
  than an empty one taking up space.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign chip_source = chips | default: '' | strip -%}
{%- if chip_source contains '|' -%}
  {%- assign chip_list = chip_source | split: '|' -%}
{%- else -%}
  {%- assign chip_list = chip_source | newline_to_br | split: '<br />' -%}
{%- endif -%}

<form
  class="non-somm{% if modifier != blank %} {{ modifier }}{% endif %}"
  data-non-somm
  data-non-somm-entry
  data-somm-context="{{ somm_context }}"
  data-somm-surface="{{ somm_surface }}"
  {%- comment -%}
    THE CONTROLLER'S HOOKS, emitted per surface.

    Found by auditing every selector in assets/*.js before retiring the old
    markup, which is the only reason this snippet works. somm-sheet.js hands
    the hero's submit to the sheet through `[data-non-somm-hero]` and reads the
    typed text from `[data-non-somm-hero-input]`; without both, the hero form
    submits, the sheet never opens, and the control is silently dead - the same
    failure mode as the welded attributes, and just as invisible.

    Scoped by surface rather than emitted everywhere: `[data-non-somm-hero]` is
    queried with querySelector, so a second element carrying it would take the
    handoff and the real hero would lose it.

    Note the JS binds NOTHING to the .non-somm-entry tree - not one selector -
    which is why retiring that component cannot break behaviour.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- if somm_surface == 'homepage_hero' %} data-non-somm-hero{% endif -%}
  {%- if product != blank %}
    data-somm-product="{{ product.id }}"
    data-somm-product-title="{{ product.title | escape }}"
    data-somm-variant="{{ product.selected_or_first_available_variant.id }}"
  {%- endif -%}
  {%- if code != blank %} data-somm-code="{{ code | escape }}"{% endif %}
  role="search">

  {%- comment -%}
    The eyebrow sits in column 2 with the rest of the content, NOT above the
    whole form: the orb spans the composition, so a label placed outside the
    grid's second column would push the orb down by its height and break the
    vertical relationship the pairing page establishes.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- if label != blank -%}
    <div class="non-mono non-eyebrow non-somm__label">{{ label }}</div>
  {%- endif -%}

  <div class="non-somm__bar">
    <span class="non-somm__caret" aria-hidden="true">&gt;</span>
    <label class="visually-hidden" for="somm-q-{{ somm_uid }}">{{ placeholder }}</label>
    <input
      id="somm-q-{{ somm_uid }}"
      class="non-somm__input"
      type="search"
      autocomplete="off"
      data-non-somm-input
      {% if somm_surface == 'homepage_hero' %}data-non-somm-hero-input{% endif %}
      placeholder="{{ placeholder | escape }}">
    <button type="submit" class="non-somm__submit">{{ submit_label }}</button>
  </div>

  {%- comment -%}
    The seeds sit INSIDE the form, as they do on the pairing page. That
    placement is load-bearing, not tidiness: every light-surface correction is
    scoped `.non-somm .non-somm__seed`, and `.non-somm__seeds` carries padding
    written to sit inside the panel. A chip outside the form matches none of
    it and falls back to a near-black pill on a near-black page.

    No data-answer, for the reason recorded in pairing-tool.liquid: it made
    the script type the label back instead of asking, so the chips looked dead.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- assign chip_count = 0 -%}
  {%- for chip in chip_list -%}
    {%- assign chip_text = chip | strip_html | strip -%}
    {%- if chip_text != blank -%}{%- assign chip_count = chip_count | plus: 1 -%}{%- endif -%}
  {%- endfor -%}

  {%- if chip_count > 0 -%}
    <div class="non-somm__seeds">
      {%- for chip in chip_list -%}
        {%- assign chip_text = chip | strip_html | strip -%}
        {%- if chip_text != blank -%}
          <button type="button" class="non-somm__seed" data-non-somm-seed>{{ chip_text }}</button>
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- endfor -%}
    </div>
  {%- endif -%}
</form>
